{"name":"Arrowwood","hex":"#b3861e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arrowwood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of genus Viburnum of eastern North America and other viburnums that have naturalized in North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrowwood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cornus florida","blocks":[{"text":"Cornus florida, the flowering dogwood or American dogwood, is a species of flowering tree in the family Cornaceae native to eastern North America and northern Mexico. An endemic population once spanned from southernmost coastal Maine south to northern Florida and west to the Mississippi River. The tree is commonly planted as an ornamental in residential and public areas because of its showy bracts and interesting bark structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Cornus_florida_Arkansas.jpg/330px-Cornus_florida_Arkansas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornus_florida","wikidata":"Q887221"},{"title":"Viburnum","blocks":[{"text":"Viburnum is a genus of about 150–175 species of flowering plants in the family Viburnaceae. Its current classification is based on molecular phylogeny. It was previously included in the family Caprifoliaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Viburnum_opulus_C.jpg/330px-Viburnum_opulus_C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viburnum","wikidata":"Q158492"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/2014-10-30_10_36_30_Flowering_Dogwood_foliage_during_autumn_on_Glen_Mawr_Drive_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG/500px-2014-10-30_10_36_30_Flowering_Dogwood_foliage_during_autumn_on_Glen_Mawr_Drive_in_Ewing%2C_New_Jersey.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed